- system_vocabulary
- http_foot
- desk
- scope
- scope_foot
- mesa_wire

' Registers the foot at /<self>/io/scope when a world starts. What the foot
' tends is said by records beneath its own (scope_foot.foil); with none it
' does nothing.
'
' And the two things a door does for a scope. It gives the link to an
' invitation, with its secret, to someone this world let in
' (/scope/link/<number>); and it is handed a link (/scope/join). In both
' the secret passes between the request and a file of the foot's and
' touches no record: the route is the only place outside the foot that
' ever holds one, for the length of one request.
'
' And one reading: a composition this world takes part in, as it stands
' for this world (/scope/view/<record>): what it holds, what is its to
' do, what it may ask and what it waits on. It writes nothing.
'
' Every act here answers through a voice: as plain text to a request, or
' wrapped for an agent's call (the agent door passes its own). So a person
' and an agent do the same things by the same rules, and neither surface
' holds a rule of its own.
+ scope_mount
  + text
    \ status=nat body=str
    ^ http_foot/action
    | ./reply (http_driver/response status body)
  + voice
    ' How an act answers: say makes the response to a request; wrap makes
    ' the status and body of one that is rendered after a commit.
    : say={\ nat str}http_response wrap={\ nat str}[nat str]
  + same
    \ status=nat body=str
    ^ [nat str]
    [status body]
  + plain
    ' The voice of a plain request: the text, as it is.
    ^ scope_mount/voice
    | scope_mount/voice http_driver/response scope_mount/same
  + number
    ' The number after a route's own name in a target, or none:
    ' /scope/link/7.
    \ prefix=str target=str
    ^ maybe[nat]
    = none=maybe[nat] .none
      url (http_foot/split 63 target).at(0)
    ? !(gt url.len prefix.len.inc) none
    | nat/parse url.slice(prefix.len.inc url.len)
  + asked
    \ v=scope_mount/voice outcome=maybe[pail]
    ^ http_response
    = say v.say
    ? outcome
     > .none (say 202 "The link is being made. Ask again.")
     > (./some why) (say 409 (http_foot/reason why))
  + linking
    ' The link to an invitation this world minted, with its secret after
    ' it, for someone this world let in. The secret is the foot's: the
    ' route asks the desk, the foot leaves the secret as a file, and the
    ' route takes it once and empties the file. So the first request is
    ' answered "being made" and a later one with the link.
    \ self=iota request=http_foot/request now=nat v=scope_mount/voice
    ^ http_foot/action
    = say v.say
    ? !(equal request.method "POST") (./reply (say 405 "POST required"))
    ? (eq 0 request.who) (./reply (say 401 "Only someone this world has let in is given a link."))
    ?> (./some id) (scope_mount/number "/scope/link" request.target) (./reply (say 400 "Name the invitation by its number: /scope/link/1"))
    | scope_mount/handing self id v
  + handing
    ' The link to the invitation of one number, handed over once.
    \ self=iota id=nat v=scope_mount/voice
    ^ http_foot/action
    = say v.say
      ask=path (desk/root self).weld(['link ($u id)])
      reader
        \ state=namespace
        ^ [nat str]
        = waiting (sovereign_care .x ask state).fil.fall((myth/sing ['done] (pails/n 1)))
        ?> (./some l) (scope_foot/invitation id state) [404 "No scope this world keeps holds a place with that invitation, or this world does not say where it is reached."]
        ? (eq 0 waiting.nat_at(['done] 0)) [202 "The link is being made. Ask again."]
        [200 (scope/show l)]
      next
        \ status=nat said=str
        ^ http_foot/action
        ? !(eq status 200) (./reply (say status said))
        = file (str/cat_all ["io/mesa/out/" (nat/show id)])
          ;held (mesa_wire/took file)
          want=myth (myth/sing ['want] (pails/t "link")).put(['id] (pails/n id))
        ? !(eq 33 (wid held)) (http_foot/action/commit ask (writ/make want) (\ outcome=maybe[pail] (scope_mount/asked v outcome)))
        = ;emptied (WriteFile file 1)
        | ./reply (say 200 (str/cat_all [said "," (nat/show held)]))
    | http_foot/action/after reader next
  + opening
    ' An open place gives whoever asks a place of their own beneath it
    ' (scope_foot/taking). The asker shows a ticket, a secret of their own
    ' making, the way a session is shown; the place keeps its hash, and
    ' the ticket is then what fetches the link (ticketing). Nobody may ask:
    ' that is what open means, and how many may is the place's to say.
    \ request=http_foot/request now=nat v=scope_mount/voice
    ^ http_foot/action
    = say v.say
      url (http_foot/split 63 request.target).at(0)
      lead=str "/door/open"
      ticket request.asked
      how=str "Name the composition and the place: /door/open/course/seats"
    ? !(equal request.method "POST") (./reply (say 405 "POST required"))
    ?> (./some rel) (path_parse url.slice(lead.len url.len)) (./reply (say 400 how))
    ? (lt rel.len 2) (./reply (say 400 how))
    = name rel.at(0)
      where=path rel.drop(1)
      plan
        \ state=namespace
        ^ either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]]
        ? (scope_foot/taking name where ticket state)
         > (./err why) (./err 'scope_shut)
         > (./ok writes) (./ok writes)
      reader
        \ state=namespace
        ^ [nat str]
        ? (scope_foot/taking name where ticket state)
         > (./err why) [409 why]
         > (./ok writes) [200 ""]
      next
        \ status=nat said=str
        ^ http_foot/action
        ? !(eq status 200) (./reply (say status said))
        | http_foot/action/admit plan (\ outcome=maybe[pail] state=namespace (scope_mount/taken v "A place is yours. Show the ticket again for its link." outcome)) scope_mount/quiet
    | http_foot/action/after reader next
  + inviting
    ' A place of a composition is given an invitation (scope_foot/
    ' inviting), by whoever this world let in. Its link is then asked for
    ' by its number, like any other.
    \ word=str place=str v=scope_mount/voice
    ^ http_foot/action
    = say v.say
    ?> (./some name) (scope_mount/named word) (./reply (say 400 "Name the composition by the record that says this world takes part in it."))
    ?> (./some where) (path_parse place) (./reply (say 400 "Name the place by its path in the composition: /seats/third"))
    = plan
        \ state=namespace
        ^ either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]]
        ? (scope_foot/inviting name where state)
         > (./err why) (./err 'scope_invite)
         > (./ok writes) (./ok writes)
      reader
        \ state=namespace
        ^ [nat str]
        ? (scope_foot/inviting name where state)
         > (./err why) [409 why]
         > (./ok writes) [200 ""]
      next
        \ status=nat said=str
        ^ http_foot/action
        ? !(eq status 200) (./reply (say status said))
        | http_foot/action/admit plan (\ outcome=maybe[pail] state=namespace (scope_mount/taken v "The place holds an invitation. Its number is on its record." outcome)) scope_mount/quiet
    | http_foot/action/after reader next
  + ticketing
    ' The link to the place taken under the ticket a request shows, with
    ' its secret, handed over once like any other (handing).
    \ self=iota request=http_foot/request now=nat v=scope_mount/voice
    ^ http_foot/action
    = say v.say
      reader
        \ state=namespace
        ^ [nat str]
        = id (scope_foot/ticket request.asked state)
        ? (eq 0 id) [404 "No place was taken under that ticket."]
        [200 (nat/show id)]
      next
        \ status=nat said=str
        ^ http_foot/action
        ? !(eq status 200) (./reply (say status said))
        ?> (./some id) (nat/parse said) (./reply (say 404 "No place was taken under that ticket."))
        | scope_mount/handing self id v
    ? !(equal request.method "POST") (./reply (say 405 "POST required"))
    | http_foot/action/after reader next
  + link
    \ self=iota request=http_foot/request now=nat
    ^ http_foot/action
    | scope_mount/linking self request now scope_mount/plain
  + view
    ' A composition this world takes part in, as it stands for this world
    ' (scope_foot/view), as lines of text, for someone this world let in.
    ' The record is named as it is beneath /<self>/io/scope.
    \ request=http_foot/request now=nat
    ^ http_foot/action
    = url (http_foot/split 63 request.target).at(0)
      lead=str "/scope/view/"
      nothing=str ""
      word=str (? (gt url.len lead.len) url.slice(lead.len url.len) nothing)
    ? !(equal request.method "GET") (scope_mount/text 405 "GET required")
    ? (eq 0 request.who) (scope_mount/text 401 "Only someone this world has let in is shown what it takes part in.")
    ?> (./some rel) (path_parse (str/cat_all ["/" word])) (scope_mount/text 400 "Name the record: /scope/view/course")
    ? !(eq 1 rel.len) (scope_mount/text 400 "Name the record: /scope/view/course")
    = name rel.at(0)
      reader
        \ state=namespace
        ^ [nat str]
        ?> (./some lines) (scope_foot/view name state) [404 "No record of that name says this world takes part in a composition."]
        [200 lines]
      next
        \ status=nat said=str
        ^ http_foot/action
        | scope_mount/text status said
    | http_foot/action/after reader next
  + refusal
    \ why=iota
    ^ [nat str]
    ? (eq_iota why 'scope_door) [401 "Only someone this world has let in may hand it that link."]
    ? (eq_iota why 'scope_joined) [409 "This world has already joined under that name."]
    ? (eq_iota why 'scope_unprepared) [409 "This world was not started under that name."]
    ? (eq_iota why 'scope_busy) [409 "A claim of that name is still being answered. Hand the link over again in a moment."]
    [409 "That is not a link this world can take."]
  + taken
    \ v=scope_mount/voice done=str outcome=maybe[pail]
    ^ [nat str]
    = wrap v.wrap
    ? outcome
     > .none (wrap 202 done)
     > (./some why) (wrap 409 (http_foot/reason why))
  + quiet
    \ outcome=maybe[pail] state=namespace
    ^ str
    ""
  + joining
    ' A link handed to this world's door, with its secret after it. The
    ' secret is left for the foot as a file, under the number of the name
    ' the link claims, and goes into no record; the door writes the ask
    ' and the record of the joining (scope/join), and the foot does the
    ' rest. Someone this world let in may hand over any link. Nobody may
    ' hand over only the link this world was prepared for, while it has
    ' let nobody in; and the session such a request showed is the one the
    ' claim lets in.
    \ request=http_foot/request now=nat v=scope_mount/voice
    ^ http_foot/action
    = say v.say
      body (http_foot/trim request.body)
      secret (scope/secret body)
      until (add now desk/year)
      session (? (eq 0 request.who) request.asked 0)
    ? !(equal request.method "POST") (./reply (say 405 "POST required"))
    ?> (./some l) (scope/read body) (./reply (say 400 "That is not a link."))
    ? !(eq 33 (wid secret)) (./reply (say 400 "The link carries no secret."))
    = handed l.name
      plan
        \ state=namespace
        ^ either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]]
        ? (and (eq 0 request.who) !(scope/unlocked l state)) (./err 'scope_door)
        | scope/join l handed session until state
      reader
        \ state=namespace
        ^ [nat str]
        ? (plan state)
         > (./err why) (scope_mount/refusal why)
         > (./ok writes) [200 ""]
      next
        \ status=nat said=str
        ^ http_foot/action
        ? !(eq status 200) (./reply (say status said))
        = ;folder (Folder "io/mesa/in")
          ;wrote (WriteFile (mesa_wire/handed handed) secret)
        | http_foot/action/admit plan (\ outcome=maybe[pail] state=namespace (scope_mount/taken v "" outcome)) scope_mount/quiet
    | http_foot/action/after reader next
  + join
    \ request=http_foot/request now=nat
    ^ http_foot/action
    | scope_mount/joining request now scope_mount/plain
  + named
    ' The one name a word spells, or none.
    \ word=str
    ^ maybe[iota]
    = none=maybe[iota] .none
    ?> (./some rel) (path_parse (str/cat_all ["/" word])) none
    ? !(eq 1 rel.len) none
    | ./some rel.at(0)
  + seen
    ' Every composition this world keeps or takes part in, each as it
    ' stands for this world (scope_foot/view) beneath a line that names it.
    ' One in which nothing is yet shown to this world is left out.
    \ state=namespace
    ^ str
    = none=row[str] []
      lines
        | (sovereign_peek (scope_foot/home state.self) state).tap.fold none
          \ acc [rel record]
          ? !(eq rel.len 1) acc
          ?> (./some said) (scope_foot/view rel.at(0) state) acc
          ? (eq 0 said.len) acc
          | acc.snoc((str/cat_all ["composition " (path_show rel)])).snoc(said)
    | str/join (str/from_atom 10) lines
  + seeing
    \ v=scope_mount/voice
    ^ http_foot/action
    = wrap v.wrap
    | ./snapshot (\ state=namespace (wrap 200 (scope_mount/seen state)))
  + packing
    ' The packs this world holds (scope_foot/packs).
    \ v=scope_mount/voice
    ^ http_foot/action
    = wrap v.wrap
    | ./snapshot (\ state=namespace (wrap 200 (scope_foot/packs state)))
  + shaped
    \ name=iota v=scope_mount/voice state=namespace
    ^ [nat str]
    = wrap v.wrap
    ?> (./some lines) (scope_foot/shape name state) (wrap 404 "No record of that name says this world takes part in a composition.")
    | wrap 200 lines
  + shaping
    ' The table of one composition, a line a row, with the slots a record
    ' at each row may hold (scope_foot/shape).
    \ word=str v=scope_mount/voice
    ^ http_foot/action
    = say v.say
    ?> (./some name) (scope_mount/named word) (./reply (say 400 "Name the composition by the record that says this world takes part in it."))
    | ./snapshot (\ state=namespace (scope_mount/shaped name v state))
  + one
    \ target=path record=myth
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    [[target (writ/make record)]]
  + filled
    \ name=iota where=path record=myth state=namespace
    ^ either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]]
    ? (scope_foot/fill name where record state)
     > (./err why) (./err 'scope_fill)
     > (./ok target) (./ok (scope_mount/one target record))
  + fillable
    \ name=iota where=path record=myth state=namespace
    ^ [nat str]
    ? (scope_foot/fill name where record state)
     > (./err why) [409 why]
     > (./ok target) [200 (path_show target)]
  + filling
    ' A record written at a place of a composition: by whoever this world
    ' let in, where the place is this world's to write now and the record
    ' has the shape its row gives (scope_foot/fill). Filling a place and
    ' asking for an action are this one act: an ask is a record at a row
    ' that applies one. It is checked again when it is admitted.
    \ word=str place=str record=myth v=scope_mount/voice
    ^ http_foot/action
    = say v.say
    ?> (./some name) (scope_mount/named word) (./reply (say 400 "Name the composition by the record that says this world takes part in it."))
    ?> (./some where) (path_parse place) (./reply (say 400 "Name the place by its path in the composition: /items/3"))
    = next
        \ status=nat said=str
        ^ http_foot/action
        ? !(eq status 200) (./reply (say status said))
        | http_foot/action/admit (\ state=namespace (scope_mount/filled name where record state)) (\ outcome=maybe[pail] state=namespace (scope_mount/taken v said outcome)) scope_mount/quiet
    | http_foot/action/after (\ state=namespace (scope_mount/fillable name where record state)) next
  + makeable
    \ source=path target=path rel=path state=namespace
    ^ [nat str]
    ? !(maybe/is_some (sovereign_care .x source state).fil) [404 "This world holds no pack of that name."]
    ? (maybe/is_some (sovereign_care .x target state).fil) [409 "A composition of that name is already here."]
    [200 (path_show rel)]
  + made
    \ v=scope_mount/voice said=str outcome=maybe[pail]
    ^ http_response
    = say v.say
    ? outcome
     > .none (say 202 (str/cat_all ["The composition is being made at " said "."]))
     > (./some why) (say 409 (http_foot/reason why))
  + making
    ' A composition asked for from a pack this world holds: one record
    ' beneath the foot's own that names the pack and where the composition
    ' is to sit. The foot makes it (scope_foot).
    \ self=iota pack=str word=str v=scope_mount/voice
    ^ http_foot/action
    = say v.say
    ?> (./some name) (scope_mount/named word) (./reply (say 400 "Give the composition a name of one word."))
    ?> (./some unit) (scope_mount/named pack) (./reply (say 400 "Name the pack."))
    = source=path [self 'gov unit]
      target=path (scope_foot/home self).snoc(name)
      rel=path ['app name]
      record=myth (myth/sing ['make] (safe 0 .x source)).put(['rel] (pails/t (path_show rel)))
      next
        \ status=nat said=str
        ^ http_foot/action
        ? !(eq status 200) (./reply (say status said))
        | http_foot/action/commit target (writ/make record) (\ outcome=maybe[pail] (scope_mount/made v said outcome))
    | http_foot/action/after (\ state=namespace (scope_mount/makeable source target rel state)) next
  + page
    ' The door's own page: the one thing nobody is shown. It takes a
    ' session and keeps it for the browser, or takes a link, hands it over
    ' with a session it makes there, and keeps that one once the claim
    ' lets it in. Where this world keeps a place open, it offers to take
    ' one: it makes a ticket, takes the place, fetches the link with the
    ' ticket, and follows it to the world started for that place, which is
    ' reached under the same domain by its name.
    ^ str
    "<!doctype html><meta charset='utf-8'><meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width,initial-scale=1'><title>Door</title><body style='font:16px system-ui;max-width:34rem;margin:4rem auto;padding:0 1rem'><h1>Door</h1><p id='say'>Paste a link you were given, or a session.</p><input id='in' style='width:100%;padding:.5rem;box-sizing:border-box' autofocus><p><button id='go'>Enter</button></p><div id='open'></div><script>var say=document.getElementById('say');function keep(s){document.cookie='session='+s+'; path=/; max-age=31536000; SameSite=Strict'+(location.protocol==='https:'?'; Secure':'')}function made(){var a=new Uint8Array(16);crypto.getRandomValues(a);return Array.from(a).map(function(b){return ('0'+b.toString(16)).slice(-2)}).join('')}function named(n){var b=BigInt(n),s='';while(b>0n){s+=('0'+(b&255n).toString(16)).slice(-2);b>>=8n}return '0x'+s}function enter(v){v=v.trim();if(!v)return;if(v.split(',').length===12){var s=made();say.textContent='Taking the link...';fetch('/door/join',{method:'POST',headers:{'Authorization':'Bearer '+s},body:v}).then(function(r){return r.text().then(function(t){if(r.status!==202&&r.status!==200){say.textContent=t||'The link was not taken.';return}keep(s);say.textContent='Claimed. Opening...';var n=0;var w=setInterval(function(){fetch('/scope/seen').then(function(q){if(q.status===200||++n>90){clearInterval(w);location.href='/home'}})},2000)})})}else{keep(v);location.href='/home'}}function follow(l){var h=location.hostname,d=h.split('.').slice(1).join('.');if(!d||/^[0-9.]+$/.test(h)){say.textContent='Your link, to hand to the door of the world started for it: '+l;return}location.href=location.protocol+'//'+named(l.split(',')[6])+'.'+d+'/door#'+encodeURIComponent(l)}function take(c,p){var t=made();say.textContent='Taking a place...';fetch('/door/open'+c+p,{method:'POST',headers:{'Authorization':'Bearer '+t}}).then(function(r){return r.text().then(function(x){if(r.status!==202&&r.status!==200){say.textContent=x||'No place was given.';return}say.textContent='A world of your own is being made. This can take a few minutes; keep this page open.';var w=setInterval(function(){fetch('/door/ticket',{method:'POST',headers:{'Authorization':'Bearer '+t}}).then(function(q){return q.text().then(function(l){if(q.status===200){clearInterval(w);follow(l)}})})},3000)})})}document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){enter(document.getElementById('in').value)};if(location.hash.length>1){var h=decodeURIComponent(location.hash.slice(1));history.replaceState(null,'',location.pathname);enter(h)}else{fetch('/door/open').then(function(r){return r.status===200?r.text():''}).then(function(x){var o=document.getElementById('open');x.split(String.fromCharCode(10)).forEach(function(line){var f=line.split(String.fromCharCode(9));if(f.length<5)return;var b=document.createElement('button');b.textContent='Start '+(f[4]||f[3]||f[0].slice(1));b.style.cssText='display:block;margin:.5rem 0;padding:.5rem';b.onclick=function(){take(f[0],f[1])};if(!o.firstChild){var p=document.createElement('p');p.textContent='Or, with no link:';o.appendChild(p)}o.appendChild(b)})})}</script>"
  + door
    ' The door: its page, and what nobody may do. Hand this world the link
    ' it was prepared for (/door/join). See which places this world keeps
    ' open (/door/open), take one under a ticket (/door/open/<composition>/
    ' <place>), and fetch its link with the ticket (/door/ticket).
    \ self=iota request=http_foot/request now=nat
    ^ http_foot/action
    = url (http_foot/split 63 request.target).at(0)
      opens=str "/door/open/"
    ? (equal[str] url "/door/join") (scope_mount/joining request now scope_mount/plain)
    ? (equal[str] url "/door/ticket") (scope_mount/ticketing self request now scope_mount/plain)
    ? (and (gt url.len opens.len) (equal[str] url.slice(0 opens.len) opens)) (scope_mount/opening request now scope_mount/plain)
    ? !(equal request.method "GET") (scope_mount/text 405 "GET required")
    ? (equal[str] url "/door/open") (./snapshot (\ state=namespace (scope_mount/same 200 (scope_foot/offers state))))
    | ./reply (http_response 200 (str/to_atom scope_mount/page) "text/html; charset=utf-8")
  + shown
    \ request=http_foot/request now=nat
    ^ http_foot/action
    | scope_mount/seeing scope_mount/plain
  + homed
    ' The page a person is shown once this world has let them in: one
    ' file of this mount's. It reads what an agent reads and does what an
    ' agent does, through the agent door, and holds no rule of its own.
    \ files=row[[str nat]] request=http_foot/request now=nat
    ^ http_foot/action
    = matches (files.keep((\ [key bytes] (eq key "home.html"))))
    ? !(equal request.method "GET") (scope_mount/text 405 "GET required")
    ? (eq matches.len 0) (scope_mount/text 404 "This world has no home page.")
    = [name bytes] matches.at(0)
    | ./bytes 200 bytes "text/html; charset=utf-8"
  + http
    \ files=row[[str nat]] state=namespace
    ^ http_foot/config
    = self=iota state.self
      link
        \ request=http_foot/request now=nat
        ^ http_foot/action
        | scope_mount/link self request now
      door
        \ request=http_foot/request now=nat
        ^ http_foot/action
        | scope_mount/door self request now
      home
        \ request=http_foot/request now=nat
        ^ http_foot/action
        | scope_mount/homed files request now
    | http_foot/add_routes [(http_foot/route "/home" home) (http_foot/route "/scope/link" link) (http_foot/route "/scope/join" scope_mount/join) (http_foot/route "/scope/view" scope_mount/view) (http_foot/route "/scope/seen" scope_mount/shown) (http_foot/route "/door" door)] http_foot/empty
  + accepted
    \ reply=feet/task[unit]
    ^ bool
    ? reply
     > (./ack err)
      ? err
       > .none .true
       > (./some _) .false
    .false
  + submit
    ' One write, and whether the world took it.
    \ server=nat target=path change=writ
    ^ bool
    ; (SendCaps server (helm/card/step target change) [0])
    = ;[reply caps] (Recv[feet/task[unit]] 0)
    ; (helm/supervisor/close_caps caps)
    | scope_mount/accepted reply
  + present
    ' The foot's record, made empty when the world has none. One that is
    ' there is left exactly as it is.
    \ server=nat target=path
    ^ bool
    ? (scope_mount/submit server target (writ/poke myth/new)) .true
    | scope_mount/submit server target (writ/make myth/new)
  + hand
    ' Register a pack's own hand: a foot at a home of its own that runs
    ' one rule (scope_foot/tend). The pack's mount calls this from its
    ' start with the rule, and that is the whole of what a pack writes to
    ' have a hand.
    \ server=nat home=path rule={\ namespace}row[[p=path q=writ]]
    ^ nat
    ? !(scope_mount/present server home)
      (error (pails/t "A hand's record was refused"))
    = run
        \ init=feet/task/init self=nat
        ^ nat
        | scope_foot/tend rule init self
      registration | helm/supervisor/register home run .true
    ; (SendCaps server registration [0])
    = ;[reply caps] | Recv[feet/task[unit]] 0
    ; | helm/supervisor/close_caps caps
    ? !(scope_mount/accepted reply)
      (error (pails/t "A hand's registration failed"))
    0
  + start
    \ server=nat self=iota arguments=row[str]
    ^ nat
    = home=path [self 'io 'scope]
    ? !(scope_mount/present server home)
      (error (pails/t "Scope foot record refused"))
    = registration | helm/supervisor/register home scope_foot/run .true
    ; (SendCaps server registration [0])
    = ;[reply caps] | Recv[feet/task[unit]] 0
    ; | helm/supervisor/close_caps caps
    ? !(scope_mount/accepted reply)
      (error (pails/t "Scope foot registration failed"))
    0
